        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What is params in a Brevo transactional email?</summary>
          <p>In the send request, Brevo takes a JSON object called params next to the template ID. The template reads each value with a tag such as {{ params.customerName }}. This post uses that pattern.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Why look at the whole system instead of just the template?</summary>
          <p>Because the problems in this project sat in different stages. A layout bug was in the template, a possible name mismatch was in the data, and a card number could come from the client's system. Checking only the template would have missed the data problems, so I check each stage on its own.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Should a payment receipt email contain a full card number?</summary>
          <p>No. The receipt in this project shows only the last digits, and my check refuses any value that looks like a full card number. That is my own safeguard, not a compliance standard, so check the rules that apply to your client.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How was this template checked?</summary>
          <p>Stage by stage. It compiles in MJML's strict mode, and when rendered with the original email's data its 47 lines of visible text match the original. A script checks the names and values, I rendered the layout and looked at it, and I did a real test send through Brevo and checked the delivered email in real email apps. I have not checked every app and version.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

